---
description: Load for auth, Telegram initData, admin roles, user/location data, uploads, scoring, or security reviews.
alwaysApply: false
---
- Verify Telegram WebApp `initData` on the server using the official algorithm; enforce freshness and constant-time hash comparison.
- Derive user identity only from verified initData. Never trust `initDataUnsafe`, client user IDs, locations, rewards, or scores.
- Enforce authentication, role, ownership, and object-level authorization on every protected endpoint (prevent IDOR).
- Validate inputs, rate-limit sensitive actions, and make reward/collection endpoints idempotent.
- Keep bot tokens and secrets server-side; never print `.env`, tokens, raw initData, or sensitive coordinates.
- Minimize location retention; do not upload camera frames unless a separately justified, consented feature requires it.
- Audit sensitive admin actions. Do not claim absolute security; document residual risks and tested controls.
